{"availability":"available","full":"caaatisgood/metabase-school","name":"metabase-school","description":"A Metabase-integrated, real-time collaborative tool for writing SQL","category":"Education","language":"TypeScript","stars":42,"forks":3,"created":"2021-03-09T16:15:17Z","updated":"2021-05-03T16:13:15Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://metabase-school.netlify.app/","topics":["learning","metabase","sql-editor"],"demo":"https://metabase-school.netlify.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:35:11.032Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:35:11.032Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:35:11.032Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T21:08:40.313Z","stars":42,"forks":3},{"at":"2026-10-09T03:35:11.032Z","stars":42,"forks":3}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Almost a year ago (around Jan 2020), some folks from my company (Arc & Codementor), who are good at writing SQL, decided to start an entry-level SQL class for everyone. We had a few classes where everyone will listen to the SQL experts, and then go to one of our frequently used querying tool, Redash, for practice. That's how \"SQL master class\" started. Everything happened in the same meeting room, face-to-face, like a computer class in college.","Then COVID-19 hit, and we transitioned to a fully remote work policy. We immediately found it difficult to sustain \"SQL master class\" remotely. The remote tools we used (a.k.a., Zoom or Google Meet) didn't allow the SQL experts to understand everyone's learning status at any given time the way they could in a non-remote environment. Colleagues who were struggling with getting the query right couldn't get immediate help — there's just too high of a barrier to sharing queries with one another remotely.","That's how \"Metabase School\" was born. It's a real-time collaborative editor, integrated with the Metabase API, which lets multiple people write, view, and execute queries together."],"features":["Real-time collaborative editor, made with Firebase Realtime Database, Firepad, Monaco Editor and @monaco-editor/react.","Integrated Metabase API, which enables you to query directly from your own Metabase."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/caaatisgood/metabase-school/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"32b32b7e661929a8ec71adb72d9d71bf66a3df401bedbd7a7cef248085846f06","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:40.447Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:40.447Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Almost a year ago (around Jan 2020), some folks from my company (Arc & Codementor), who are good at writing SQL, decided to start an entry-level SQL class for everyone. We had a few classes where everyone will listen to the SQL experts, and then go to one of our frequently used querying tool, Redash, for practice. That's how \"SQL master class\" started. Everything happened in the same meeting room, face-to-face, like a computer class in college.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/caaatisgood/metabase-school/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"hosting","status":"optional","text":"Decide if you want to self-host Metabase School","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/caaatisgood/metabase-school/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Login with the exact credential you used for your Metabase, and you're good to go!","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/caaatisgood/metabase-school/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Login with the exact credentials you use for your Metabase, and you're good to go!","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/caaatisgood/metabase-school/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"32b32b7e661929a8ec71adb72d9d71bf66a3df401bedbd7a7cef248085846f06","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/caaatisgood/metabase-school/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T21:08:40.447Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2021-05-03T16:13:15Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/caaatisg